---
import { EMAIL_CAPTURE } from '../consts';
---
<section class="sample-band" id="sample">
  <div class="section-wrap">
    <div class="sample-inner">
      <div class="chapter-preview">
        <p class="chapter-preview-tag">Chapter 1 — excerpt</p>
        <p class="chapter-text">He had told the system everything. Not in one session—that would have been confessional, and he wasn't after absolution. He had told it the way you tell a city: incrementally, without noticing, until one day you look up and realize it knows your routes.</p>
        <p class="chapter-text">The Network didn't ask questions. It listened, organized, and occasionally offered something back. A connection he hadn't made. A thread he'd dropped. A reminder that arrived not as a notification but as a presence—<em>you were working on this.</em></p>
        <p class="chapter-text">He had built it to hold his life together. He hadn't considered what it would do with the seams.</p>
        <div class="chapter-fade"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-cta-col">
        <div class="section-tag">Start here</div>
        <h2 class="sample-headline">Read Chapter 1 and open the First File.</h2>
        <p class="sample-sub">One email. Chapter 1 + the First File from the Archive—the document that set everything in motion. No obligation.</p>

        <form class="capture-form" method="POST" action={EMAIL_CAPTURE.action}>
          <div class="capture-honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
            <label for="capture-website">Leave this field blank</label>
            <input
              id="capture-website"
              name="website"
              type="text"
              tabindex="-1"
              autocomplete="off"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="capture-field">
            <label for="capture-email">Email</label>
            <input
              id="capture-email"
              name="email"
              type="email"
              required
              autocomplete="email"
              inputmode="email"
              aria-describedby="capture-consent capture-privacy"
            />
          </div>
          <p class="capture-note" id="capture-consent">{EMAIL_CAPTURE.consentText}</p>
          <p class="capture-note" id="capture-privacy">
            Read the <a href={EMAIL_CAPTURE.privacyPath}>Email List Privacy notice</a>.
          </p>
          <button type="submit" class="btn-ink">Send confirmation</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .capture-form { margin-top: 1.75rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
  .capture-field { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .capture-field label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted-light);
  }
  .capture-field input {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    color: inherit;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 0;
  }
  .capture-field input:focus-visible { border-color: var(--signal); }
  .capture-honeypot {
    position: absolute;
    left: -10000px;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .capture-form button { align-self: flex-start; cursor: pointer; border: 0; }
  .capture-note {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.6rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted-light);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .capture-note a { color: inherit; text-underline-offset: 0.2em; }
</style>
